UID:120441-1778320800-1778328000@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Great Sunflower Project
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators are beautiful\, fascinating\, and crucial members of Piedmont ecosystems\, and spring is a wonderful time to observe and learn from them! As global change threatens insect populations worldwide\, it is more important than ever that we monitor these important species. Come be a part of this effort\, as we learn about the pollinators that live at Prairie Ridge\, look for them around the Ecostation\, and contribute observations to The Great Sunflower Project\, a collaborative science project supporting active pollinator research\, education\, and conservation. Come dressed for the weather and ready for about a half-mile walk for this program for ages 8+. \nRegistration is required to attend this program. \nRegister
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/great-sunflower-project-2/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Children,Citizen Science,Educators,K-12 Students,Outdoor Experiences,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Lucie%20Ciccone":MAILTO:lucie.ciccone@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.812182885871;-78.713963528554
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Prairie Ridge 1671 Gold Star Drive Raleigh NC 27607 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1671 Gold Star Drive:geo:-78.713963528554,35.812182885871
END:VEVENT
